  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Interagency Standing Committee (IASC) Steering Committee Review of the IASC Community-Based Complaints Mechanism (CBCM) Approach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Inter-Agency Standing Committee (IASC) approach to inter-agency (IA) community-based complaints mechanisms (CBCM) was developed by an inter-agency Steering Group and endorsed by the IASC Principals following a 2010 IASC external review on protection from sexual exploitation and abuse (PSEA). In 2021, the IASC External Review of Protection from Sexual Exploitation and Abuse and Sexual Harassment highlighted that 10 years later there were challenges with the approach and lack of sustained resourcing at global and country level to IA-CBCMs and that adaption and updating were needed. In the recommendations of the External Review, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) was tasked to propose a way forward on the inter-agency process to assess the application and effectiveness of the CBCM approach, and to support a collective process to revise the approach and guidance accordingly. Through this project, IOM is supporting resourcing required to ensure these deliverables are developed efficiently and input from the Steering Committee is maximized and consultative. In addition, consultations with field practitioners are being coordinated and conducted to ensure the tools are relevant and needs-based.</narrative>
  </description>
